From 1468d99cbbbcaad6f87a0b4a8051896103c28308 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: opencode <user@example.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 09:49:18 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 13/29] turnip/a5xx: first working Vulkan triangle (sysmem)

- Emit RB_BLEND_CNTL with SAMPLE_MASK(0xffff): a zero sample mask
  means no covered samples, so the FS was never launched even though
  the VS ran and VPC looked correct.
- Use the fd5 colour swap table: R8G8B8A8 -> WZYX, B8G8R8A8 -> WXYZ.
- Set BYPASS render mode via CP_SET_RENDER_MODE for sysmem rendering.
- Enable HLSQ VS/FS SSBO_ENABLE when the shader has SSBOs.
- Add TU5_GFX_DUMPCS debug dump and extra TU5_GFX_DEBUG state output.

tu5_fsprobe_test: probe=0x87654321, all 4096 pixels red -> PASS.
